COMMAND NAME: mppsizecalc.sh

Shows the disk space usage for a given database, table, or index.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppsizecalc.sh {-x <database_name> | {-t <schema.table_name> [-h] [-i] 
[-a <database_name>]}} [-d <master_data_directory>] [-s b|k|m] [-f]  
[-l <logfile_directory>][-p | -m] [-D] [-q] [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppsizecalc.sh script can be used to determine the disk space usage for 
a Greenplum database, table, or index. mppsizecalc.sh displays the following 
information:

* The total disk space usage for the specified database.

* The total disk space usage for the specified table. Note that for 
  partitioned parent tables, it will not show sizing information for 
  its child tables. You must inquire about child tables directly.

* The total disk space usage for the specified table’s index.

* The disk usage per active segment (if -f option is supplied).

*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-x <database_name>

Either a database name or a table name is required. The database for 
which you want to see the disk space usage.

-t <schema.table_name>

Either a database name or a table name is required. The schema qualified 
table name for which you want to see the disk space usage.

-h (show child table hierarchy)

Optional. If the table supplied with the -t option has child tables 
associated with it, this option will show information for the 
inherited child tables as well.

-i (show index size)

Optional. Shows the index size for the named table.

-a <database_name_for _table>

Optional. The name of the database for the specified table. If not 
supplied, the script uses the default database (which is the most 
recently created database).

-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The master host data directory. If not specified, the value set 
for $MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.

-s b | k | m (display bytes, kilobytes, or megabytes)

Optional. Display disk usage size information in bytes (b), kilobytes (k), 
or megabytes (m). The default is kilobytes (k).

-f (per segment)

Optional. Displays the disk space usage per segment.

-p (primary segments only)

Obtain sizing information for primary segments only.

-m (mirror segments only)

Obtain sizing information for mirror segments only.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-D (show detailed output)

Optional. If supplied will output all script log messages to the screen.

-q (no screen output)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, but 
is still written to the log file.

-? (help)

Displays the online help.

-v (show script version)

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Show the total disk space usage for a table:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products

Show the total disk space usage for a database. Show size in megabytes 
rather than kilobytes:

mppsizecalc.sh -x gpdb -s m

Show the disk space usage per segment for a table:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products -f

Show the disk space usage per segment for a database:

mppsizecalc.sh -x gpdb -f

Show the index sizes for a table that is in another database besides the 
default:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products -a gpdb2 -i


